{"scripts/test-gcal-webhooks.sh uses sed -i '' which is macOS-specific and fails with GNU sed on Linux": 0.9217749238014221, "CredentialActionsDropdown's deleteCache mutation never invalidates/refetches viewer.calendars.connectedCalendars, so the dropdown continues to show the old cacheUpdatedAt after a successful delete": 0.9425380825996399, "apps/web's dev:cron script uses npx tsx but tsx is not declared in the workspace's dependencies, making the script non-reproducible and dependent on external network/tooling state": 0.884674072265625, "deleteCacheHandler throws a plain Error when a credential is missing/unauthorized instead of a typed TRPCError with NOT_FOUND/UNAUTHORIZED code, preventing clients from distinguishing auth failures from server failures": 0.8165642619132996, "connectedCalendarsHandler directly instantiates CalendarCacheRepository bypassing the CalendarCache.init feature-flag gate, causing an extra DB query even when the calendar-cache feature is globally disabled": 0.8063151240348816, "GoogleCalendarService.fetchAvailabilityAndSetCache runs SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId after refreshing cache, adding an extra database write on webhook-driven paths which can increase DB write load proportionally to webhook volume": 0.5939251184463501}